FFmpeg 9.0.2 vulkan: an execution's fence is reset at submission, so one that is never submitted is not waited on forever

ff_vk_exec_start() waited for the execution context's fence and reset it at once; the submission that signals it
again comes later, in ff_vk_exec_submit(). When anything between the two fails - vkEndCommandBuffer returning an
error, an error while recording, a failed vkQueueSubmit2 - the context is left with an unsignalled fence that nothing
will signal, and the next ff_vk_exec_start() on it (the pool hands its contexts out round robin), ff_vk_exec_wait()
or ff_vk_exec_pool_free() (after an earlier submission) waits with UINT64_MAX: the decoder hangs. Seen on an Arc
B580 (13 Nov 2026) with a Mesa build that refused out-of-range DPB slots by failing vkEndCommandBuffer
(VK_ERROR_INVALID_VIDEO_STD_PARAMETERS_KHR): the HEVC streams RPS_B/C/E_qualcomm/ericsson and the H.264 streams
HCBP2/HCMP1_HHI_A hung after the first refused picture instead of losing it.

The fence is now reset in ff_vk_exec_submit() right before vkQueueSubmit2, and replaced with a signalled one if the
submission fails (a failed vkQueueSubmit2 leaves it as it was: unsignalled). An execution that is started and
abandoned therefore keeps a signalled fence. FFmpeg master was not checked.

--- a/libavutil/vulkan.c
+++ b/libavutil/vulkan.c
@@ -598,9 +598,12 @@
         .flags = VK_COMMAND_BUFFER_USAGE_ONE_TIME_SUBMIT_BIT,
     };
 
-    /* Wait for the fence to be signalled */
+    /* Wait for the fence to be signalled. It is reset in ff_vk_exec_submit(),
+     * right before the submission that signals it again: an execution that
+     * is started but never submitted (vkEndCommandBuffer failed, an error
+     * while recording) leaves it signalled, and the next ff_vk_exec_start()
+     * or ff_vk_exec_wait() on this context does not wait forever. */
     vk->WaitForFences(s->hwctx->act_dev, 1, &e->fence, VK_TRUE, UINT64_MAX);
-    vk->ResetFences(s->hwctx->act_dev, 1, &e->fence);
 
     /* Discard queue dependencies */
     ff_vk_exec_discard_deps(s, e);
@@ -973,6 +976,8 @@
         ff_vk_exec_discard_deps(s, e);
         return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
     }
+
+    vk->ResetFences(s->hwctx->act_dev, 1, &e->fence);
 
 #if FF_API_VULKAN_SYNC_QUEUES
 FF_DISABLE_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS
@@ -987,9 +992,20 @@
 #endif
 
     if (ret != VK_SUCCESS) {
+        VkFenceCreateInfo fence_create = {
+            .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_FENCE_CREATE_INFO,
+            .flags = VK_FENCE_CREATE_SIGNALED_BIT,
+        };
         av_log(s, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Unable to submit command buffer: %s\n",
                ff_vk_ret2str(ret));
         ff_vk_exec_discard_deps(s, e);
+        /* A failed submission leaves the fence unsignalled (reset above):
+         * replace it with a signalled one, so nothing waits on it forever. */
+        vk->DestroyFence(s->hwctx->act_dev, e->fence, s->hwctx->alloc);
+        e->fence = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
+        if (vk->CreateFence(s->hwctx->act_dev, &fence_create, s->hwctx->alloc,
+                            &e->fence) != VK_SUCCESS)
+            e->fence = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
         return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
     }
 
